---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { baseUrl } from '../../utils/base.ts';
---

<Layout
  title="Try - UOMP"
  description="One uomp setup command imports notes, writes the client config, and starts the background server. The first request comes from the agent, and UOMP opens a local approval page. Packaging the CLI is next."
  lang="en"
  switchHref={`${baseUrl}try/`}
>
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h1 style="margin-bottom:.25rem">Try UOMP</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--mid);max-width:620px;line-height:1.65">
        Today one <code>uomp setup</code> command imports Markdown notes, starts the background server, and writes the Claude Desktop / Cursor / OpenCode config. It does not pre-authorize anything.
        When you ask the client for notes, the agent requests access and UOMP opens a local approval page. Packaging the CLI and broader client validation are next.
        Both share <code style="font-size:.88rem">@uomp/sdk</code>, the Token system, Guard auth, and audit logs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="container" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:2rem;flex-wrap:wrap">

        <!-- MCP Card -->
        <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:320px;order:2">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">
            <span style="font-size:2rem">🔌</span>
            <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:1.35rem">MCP Client</h2>
          </div>
          <p style="color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:.75rem;max-width:420px">
            Claude Desktop, Cursor, or any MCP client connects over stdio; <code>uomp setup</code> writes the client config, while read access is requested by the agent and approved on the local consent page.
          </p>
          <div style="background:var(--violet-bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:.75rem 1rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--violet)">
            <strong>Experimental.</strong> Available now: <code>uomp setup claude</code>; the first tool call opens the local approval page. Claude Desktop / Cursor validation is still in progress.
          </div>
          <div style="background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem">
            <div style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Intended workflow</div>
            <div style="font-size:.85rem;color:var(--mid);line-height:1.8">
              1. Point UOMP at an Obsidian vault with <code>uomp setup claude --vault</code><br/>
              2. Ask the client for <code>notes/projects/**</code><br/>
              3. UOMP opens the approval page: scope, duration, per-key high-sensitivity<br/>
              4. After approval the agent continues; every read is checked and logged<br/>
              5. Revoke — the next request returns <code>403</code>
            </div>
          </div>
          <a href={`${baseUrl}en/tutorial/`} style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;padding:.65rem 1.5rem;background:#7C3AED;border-radius:8px;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem">
            MCP setup →
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- CLI Card -->
        <div class="card" style="flex:1;min-width:320px;order:1;border-color:var(--violet);border-width:2px">
          <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">
            <span style="font-size:2rem">⌨️</span>
            <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:1.35rem">Try with CLI</h2>
          </div>
          <p style="color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:1.25rem;max-width:400px">
            Works today. Import Obsidian/Markdown notes and grant a local agent a time-limited, revocable session.
          </p>
          <div style="background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:.75rem">
            <div style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:.4rem;font-weight:600">Quick commands</div>
            <pre style="font-size:.8rem;color:var(--mid);line-height:1.75;overflow-x:auto;background:transparent;margin:0"><code>curl -fsSL https://www.uomp.org/install.sh | bash
uomp setup claude --vault ~/Obsidian/MyVault
uomp status
uomp pending
uomp revoke &lt;id&gt;</code></pre>
          </div>
          <p style="color:var(--mid);font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:1.25rem">
            <code>setup</code> only imports notes, starts the background server, and writes the client config; it grants nothing. The first client request opens the approval page; <code>pending</code> / <code>approve</code> are the terminal fallback. Use <code>status</code> / <code>stop</code> to manage the server.
          </p>
          <a href={`${baseUrl}en/tutorial/`} style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;padding:.65rem 1.5rem;background:#233E33;border-radius:2px;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:500;font-size:.9rem">
            CLI Tutorial →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Shared infrastructure -->
    <div class="container" style="margin-top:3.5rem">
      <div class="card" style="max-width:760px">
        <h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.75rem">Shared Infrastructure</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--mid);font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.7">
          CLI and MCP are <strong>two interfaces to the same implementation</strong>. Both share <code>@uomp/sdk</code>, <code>@uomp/core</code>, the Capability Token system, Guard auth, and audit logs. Today <code>setup</code> handles one-time wiring, and the agent requests access when it needs data; next comes broader client validation and a packaged CLI.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SDK Quick Reference -->
    <div class="container" style="margin-top:3.5rem">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.15rem;margin-bottom:.5rem">Build Your Own Agent</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--mid);margin-bottom:1.5rem">For agent developers, integrate via <code>@uomp/sdk</code>:</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Sub-client</th><th>Method</th><th>Description</th></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uomp.memory</code></td><td><code>get</code>, <code>getByTag</code>, <code>getByKeys</code></td><td>Read user data</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uomp.memory</code></td><td><code>set</code>, <code>delete</code></td><td>Write (requires auth)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uomp.aggregate</code></td><td><code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>count</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>max</code></td><td>Aggregate queries</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uomp.payload</code></td><td><code>upload</code>, <code>download</code></td><td>Upload / download reports</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uomp.session</code></td><td><code>submitDeletionProof</code>, <code>finalize</code></td><td>Deletion proof + close session</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uomp.auth</code></td><td><code>createSession</code>, <code>grant</code>, <code>revoke</code></td><td>Session management</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>uomp.audit</code></td><td><code>query</code></td><td>Audit log</td></tr>
      </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-btns" style="margin-top:3rem">
      <a href="https://github.com/0xSynapse/uomp-core/tree/main/examples/stock-analyst" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-h1" style="background:#059669">Stock Analyst Source →</a>
      <a href={`${baseUrl}en/tutorial/`} class="btn-h1">SDK Tutorial →</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/0xSynapse/uomp-core" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-h2">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
